(1) the weight dichotomy, computed for several cycle types
    1^0 2^21     orbits 441  nonzero weights  1722  max weight 1  weights above 1: 0
    1^2 2^20     orbits 441  nonzero weights  1682  max weight 2  weights above 1: 40
    1^6 9^4      orbits 109  nonzero weights  1386  max weight 9  weights above 1: 168
    1^0 2^1 4^10 orbits 221  nonzero weights  1642  max weight 2  weights above 1: 80
    argument: a weight above 1 needs two pairs of one orbit at the same vertex v,
    which for a cyclic action forces v to be fixed; a fixed-point-free involution has none.

